 "dialogues": {
  "maud": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Sir Aldous. The temple has kept your family's chapel for a hundred years. Now we hear Sir Orrin is riding again, and the people ask me whether the saint has turned against them.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "He's not a saint, Mother. He's my great-grandfather, and somebody has dug him up.",
     "next": "c"
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "Then the temple will help you put him back. Tell me what you need. We have a little silver, and a few priests who can still hold a lamp steady.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "The silver. I need lancers more than prayers.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "maud_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "maud_silver"
        },
        {
         "res": {
          "gold": 400
         }
        }
       ],
       "next": "silver"
      },
      {
       "text": "Send me your priests.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "maud_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "maud_priests"
        },
        {
         "spawn": "chapel_priests"
        }
       ],
       "next": "priests"
      }
     ]
    },
    "silver": {
     "text": "It was meant for the roof. The roof can wait. Go with the saint, whatever he is now."
    },
    "priests": {
     "text": "Brother Anselm's best two. They'll keep your men standing longer than any silver would."
    }
   }
  },
  "maud_after": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "We pray for you at every bell, my lord. And for him."
    }
   }
  },
  "wat_hiding": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "...not yet, not yet, they're still in the village... get them out first, my lord..."
    }
   }
  },
  "wat": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "My lord! I'm Wat, dikereeve of Fenwick. Was. The dead closed the sluices on the north and south dikes and let the meres come up over the fields. They like it wet.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "Their riders come out of the drowned dikes. Open the sluices and the water goes down, and the riders have nowhere to hide. I know the old sluice gates, my lord. I could help, or I could take my people north where it's dry.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "Help Greyhold, Wat. Your people can work here.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "wat_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "wat_helps"
        },
        {
         "spawn": "dike_crew"
        },
        {
         "remove": "wat"
        }
       ],
       "next": "help"
      },
      {
       "text": "Take your people north. This is soldiers' work.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "wat_decided"
        },
        {
         "flag": "wat_gone"
        },
        {
         "leave": "wat",
         "to": "greyhold"
        },
        {
         "marks": 30
        }
       ],
       "next": "go"
      }
     ]
    },
    "help": {
     "text": "Then my lads will dig for you. Mind the sluice gates: the dead have chained them, but chains rust."
    },
    "go": {
     "text": "Gods keep you, my lord. Take this, it's what the village had put by. We won't need it in Greyhold."
    }
   }
  },
  "wat_after": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "The water's going down. You can smell the fields again."
    }
   }
  },
  "orrin_parley": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "who": "orrin",
     "text": "Who rides in my colours? Come closer. My eyes are... not what they were.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "Aldous Wren, lord of Greyhold. Your great-grandson.",
     "next": "c"
    },
    "c": {
     "who": "orrin",
     "text": "Greyhold. I held a gate once. I held it until the stone came down behind me. There was a boy. My son, Edric. He was in the keep when I rode out. Did he live?",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "He lived. He held Greyhold after you, and his son after him.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "orrin_told"
        }
       ],
       "next": "told"
      },
      {
       "text": "You don't get to ask about the living any more.",
       "next": "cold"
      }
     ]
    },
    "told": {
     "who": "orrin",
     "text": "Then it was worth it. ...It is hard to think, boy. Something is in my head that is not me. It says ride, and I ride. Cut me down quickly.",
     "next": "end"
    },
    "cold": {
     "who": "orrin",
     "text": "No. No, I suppose I don't. Something speaks in my head now, and it says ride.",
     "next": "end"
    },
    "end": {
     "who": "orrin",
     "text": "Knights of the Rest! To me!"
    }
   }
  }
 },
